[Library "Caro-Kann Defense"]
[Side "black"]
[Description "A rock-solid answer to 1.e4: challenge the center with ...d5 while keeping the light-squared bishop free."]
[Event "Classical: 3.Nc3"]

1. e4 c6 {Preparing ...d5 with pawn support.} 2. d4 d5 3. Nc3 (3. Nd2 dxe4 4. Nxe4 {Transposes.}) dxe4 4. Nxe4 Bf5 {The point of the Caro-Kann: the bishop gets out before ...e6.} 5. Ng3 Bg6 6. h4 {Threatening h5 to trap the bishop.} h6 7. Nf3 Nd7 8. h5 Bh7 9. Bd3 Bxd3 10. Qxd3 e6 {A solid, healthy position for Black.} *

[Library "Caro-Kann Defense"]
[Side "black"]
[Event "Advance: 3.e5"]

1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. e5 {Gaining space.} Bf5 {Again, the bishop gets out first.} 4. Nf3 (4. Nc3 e6 5. g4 Bg6 6. Nge2 c5 {Striking back at the center.}) e6 5. Be2 c5 {The thematic break against White's chain.} 6. O-O Nc6 7. c3 cxd4 8. cxd4 Nge7 {Heading for f5 to pressure d4.} *

[Library "Caro-Kann Defense"]
[Side "black"]
[Event "Exchange: 3.exd5"]

1. e4 c6 2. d4 d5 3. exd5 cxd5 4. Bd3 Nc6 5. c3 Nf6 6. Bf4 Bg4 {Develop actively before ...e6.} 7. Qb3 Qd7 {Defends b7 calmly.} 8. Nd2 e6 9. Ngf3 Bd6 {Trade off White's good bishop.} *

[Library "Caro-Kann Defense"]
[Side "black"]
[Event "Two Knights: 2.Nc3"]

1. e4 c6 2. Nc3 d5 3. Nf3 Bg4 {Pin the knight; Black can give up the bishop pair for a solid structure.} 4. h3 Bxf3 5. Qxf3 e6 6. d4 (6. d3 Nf6 7. Bd2 Nbd7 8. g3 Bc5) Nf6 7. Bd3 dxe4 8. Nxe4 Qxd4 {Grab the pawn — White has some compensation but Black is fine.} *
